---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import {
  MessageScrollerButtons,
  MessageScrollerConversation,
  MessageScrollerHistory,
  MessageScrollerNavigation,
  MessageScrollerOpening,
  MessageScrollerStates,
  MessageScrollerStreaming,
} from "../../components/MessageScrollerDemo";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
---

<Docs
  title="Message Scroller"
  description="A chat history that follows new replies and pins each new turn."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Message Scroller</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    The scrolling column of a conversation. It opens at the newest message, pins
    each new turn under the top edge so its reply reads from the start, keeps
    your place when older messages load, and shows a jump button when there is
    more history below.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8"><MessageScrollerConversation client:only="react" /></div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="A conversation"
      code={`import {
  MessageScroller,
  MessageScrollerButton,
  MessageScrollerContent,
  MessageScrollerItem,
  MessageScrollerProvider,
  MessageScrollerViewport,
} from "@tulipfarm/sprout/message-scroller";

<div className="h-96 overflow-hidden rounded-lg border">
  <MessageScrollerProvider>
    <MessageScroller>
      <MessageScrollerViewport>
        <MessageScrollerContent>
          {messages.map((message, index) => (
            <MessageScrollerItem
              key={message.id}
              messageId={message.id}
              scrollAnchor={index === messages.length - 1}
            >
              <div className="p-4">
                <Message align={message.author === "human" ? "end" : "start"}>
                  <MessageContent>
                    <MessageBubble variant={message.author === "human" ? "default" : "secondary"}>
                      {message.text}
                    </MessageBubble>
                  </MessageContent>
                </Message>
              </div>
            </MessageScrollerItem>
          ))}
        </MessageScrollerContent>
      </MessageScrollerViewport>
      <MessageScrollerButton aria-label="Scroll to newest message" />
    </MessageScroller>
  </MessageScrollerProvider>
</div>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>MessageScroller</code> fills its parent, so give the parent a height.
      <code>MessageScrollerContent</code> spaces items 24px apart; pad inside each
      item. Give every item a stable <code>messageId</code>. Set <code
        >scrollAnchor</code
      > on the turn that should be pinned when it is added, usually the newest message
      the reader sent. A pinned turn leaves 64px of the message before it showing
      (<code>scrollPreviousItemPeek</code>).
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Streaming replies</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Follow the reply while at the end"
      code={`<MessageScrollerProvider autoScroll>
  <MessageScroller>…</MessageScroller>
  <Composer />
</MessageScrollerProvider>`}
    />
    <p>
      With <code>autoScroll</code>, growing content keeps the view at the end as
      long as the reader is there. Scrolling up with the wheel, touch, or keys
      stops following until they come back to the end. Without it, the sent turn
      is still pinned and the reply grows below it.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-6"><MessageScrollerStreaming client:only="react" /></div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Jump and read position</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Hooks"
      code={`const { scrollToMessage, scrollToStart, scrollToEnd } = useMessageScroller();
const { start, end } = useMessageScrollerScrollable();
const { visibleMessageIds, currentAnchorId } = useMessageScrollerVisibility();

scrollToMessage("m8", { align: "center", behavior: "smooth" });`}
    />
    <p>
      Call the hooks anywhere inside <code>MessageScrollerProvider</code>.
      <code>align</code> is <code>"start"</code> (the default),
      <code>"center"</code>, <code>"end"</code>, or <code>"nearest"</code>;
      <code>behavior</code> is <code>"auto"</code> (the default) or
      <code>"smooth"</code>. Each returns <code>false</code> when it can’t scroll,
      such as for an unknown id; a jump requested before any message renders waits
      for it. Visibility observes items only while a component reads it.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-6"><MessageScrollerNavigation client:only="react" /></div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Opening position</h2>
    <p>
      <code>defaultScrollPosition</code> is <code>"end"</code> (the default),
      <code>"start"</code>, or <code>"last-anchor"</code>, which pins the last
      <code>scrollAnchor</code> item. The history stays hidden until it is in place,
      so it never flashes at the top first.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-6"><MessageScrollerOpening client:only="react" /></div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Jump button</h2>
    <p>
      <code>MessageScrollerButton</code> renders a Sprout
      <code>Button</code>, <code>secondary</code> and <code>icon-sm</code> by default,
      and passes <code>variant</code> and <code>size</code> through.
      <code>direction="start"</code> moves it to the top and turns the arrow up. Pass
      children for a labeled button, or <code>render</code> for your own element.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-6"><MessageScrollerButtons client:only="react" /></div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Loading earlier messages</h2>
    <p>
      <code>preserveScrollOnPrepend</code> on the viewport is on by default: when
      items are added above, the view moves by the same amount so the message you
      are reading stays still. Turn it off to see the jump.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-6"><MessageScrollerHistory client:only="react" /></div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">States</h2>
    <p>
      Put the empty, loading, or error content inside
      <code>MessageScrollerContent</code> so the frame keeps its size. Mark the viewport
      <code>aria-busy</code> while loading.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-6"><MessageScrollerStates client:only="react" /></div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      The viewport is a focusable region named “Messages” unless you pass
      <code>aria-label</code>, so arrow keys, Page Up, Page Down, Home, and End
      scroll it. The content is a polite <code>log</code> that announces new messages.
      A hidden jump button is inert and out of the tab order; icon-only buttons read
      “Scroll to end” or “Scroll to start” unless you pass <code
        >aria-label</code
      >. The button fades and slides in over 180ms. With reduced motion set it
      only fades, and its scroll is instant.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
